--- WHAT THIS RUN ACTUALLY GRADES (named wrong implementations killed) ---
    Gradeability is NOT "two captures differing only in a setting differ in some cell". That test is
    false in both directions: LB-DEC31 reports ZERO cells differing across the day-count setting and
    still kills a no-arm port by 6,015 minor units (finding T55-N1). An all-products-identical capture
    is therefore not evidence of non-gradeability.
    counterfactuals named by GRADED vectors: 0  (0 money kills, 0 structural kills)
    kills carried by REFUSED vectors: 0, credited to NOTHING (0 corroboration claims likewise)
    kills carried by HARNESS-ERROR vectors: 0, credited to NOTHING (0 corroboration claims likewise)
        An errored vector is the strongest case of "graded nothing": a refusal is at least a
        decision about the vector, an error is the absence of one. Before A2-27 these credited
        the count above, so a run with NO implementation registered — 0 cells compared — printed
        113 kills and no UNBACKED claim at all. Reachable, not hypothetical: it is the standing
        state of cmd/conformance/impl_hook.go until a port is registered (finding A2-22-F3).
        A refusal is not a pass and not a failure: it says no discriminating vector exists here, or
        the seam is blind to the behaviour. A vector that graded nothing kills nothing, so its named
        kills do not enter the count above and do not remove a capability from the UNBACKED list.
        Until A2-22 they did both, and a refusal therefore made this report QUIETER — the one case
        with LESS evidence going silent (finding A2-19 F3).
    The two are NEVER merged. A MONEY kill separates the oracle from a wrong implementation by a
    non-zero minor-unit margin. A STRUCTURAL kill separates it by a cell that carries no money at
    all — a due date, a period boundary, a row kind, the row order — and its margin is honestly 0.
    P-02's month-end re-anchor and P-03's row ordering are graded ONLY structurally: every money
    column is identical to the baseline and the port is still wrong. A store of nothing but
    structural kills grades no amount, and this line is how a reader can tell (finding D-4).
    no graded capability is backed by a parity vector yet
    UNBACKED in_graded_domain claims: monthend.reanchor, schedule.core

--- WHAT THIS RUN DOES NOT GRADE, EVEN THOUGH IT RECORDS IT ---
    The MathContext every parity vector records — (19, HALF_UP) — is PROVENANCE AND COMPARABILITY,
    not a graded claim. T55 witnessed no shape separating precision 19 from 12, or HALF_UP from
    HALF_EVEN (29 of 36 periods agree at all of them; precision 8 does separate, 22 of 36). Recording
    the setting stays mandatory; claiming a vector PROVES it would be false.
    RATE_FACTOR: TRANSCRIBED-ROUNDED at 12 decimal places, parity status TO_BE_CAPTURED.
        a Go port diverging from the oracle in digits 13 and beyond would compare EQUAL to the transcription and pass silently. Exact rate-factor parity is therefore TO_BE_CAPTURED from the oracle, and no vector may claim it.
        the rateFactor argument asserted by checkPeriod is compared AFTER value.setScale(MoneyHelper.getMathContext().getPrecision(), MoneyHelper.getRoundingMode()) [VERIFIED: ProgressiveEMICalculatorTest.java:5241; applyMathContext at :5256-5258], and the tests mock MoneyHelper's precision to 12, so every rate factor in the corpus is a 12-decimal-place rounding of the engine's value rather than the value.
    rate-factor observations carried by this run: 0 — recorded, NEVER compared.
    money cells whose wire text is over-scaled and declared as such: 0 (T17-F5; an UNDECLARED one
        is inadmissible, because a rig that silently rounded it would grade the port against a
        number the oracle never produced).

--- CROSS-CHECK SOURCES, AND THE COLUMNS THEY DO NOT COVER (T17-F2) ---
    A second attestation of the same output corroborates only the columns it actually prints. This
    harness refuses any vector claiming corroboration a source cannot give, and prints the gap here
    so that a partial match is never read as a whole-row match.
    corroboration claims made by GRADED vectors: 0 (a further 0 are carried by REFUSED vectors and 0 by HARNESS-ERROR vectors, counted nowhere)
        The claim itself SURVIVES a refusal — a corroboration is a fact about the RECORD, checked
        offline at admission, and no refusal reason impugns it. It is scoped to the graded
        population anyway, because this report scopes by POLARITY: hazards (rate factors,
        over-scaled cells) take the widest population, SUPPORT takes the narrowest, and a
        corroboration can only ever make the corpus look better attested. Add the numbers above to
        recover the corpus total; none of them is ever hidden (A2-22, adjudicated A2-24).
